Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::blocks_per_transfer_never_truncates_the_count`.

The defect: `IdentifyNamespace::blocks_per_transfer` truncates the count to 16 bits with `as u16`
instead of refusing a count that does not fit. A unit of 65536 logical blocks then answers 0, which
`Command::read` and `Command::write` refuse with a panic.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(blocks >= 1)`.

diff --git a/src/identify.rs b/src/identify.rs
--- a/src/identify.rs
+++ b/src/identify.rs
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@
         if unit_bytes == 0 || unit_bytes & ((1 << self.logical_block_size_shift) - 1) != 0 {
             return None;
         }
-        u16::try_from(unit_bytes >> self.logical_block_size_shift).ok()
+        Some((unit_bytes >> self.logical_block_size_shift) as u16)
     }
 }
 
